# VBA modules are exported by the VBE as Windows-1252 (ANSI) text with CRLF
# line endings.  Treating them as binary keeps Git from normalising either one:
# a UTF-8 round-trip would corrupt single-byte characters such as 0x80 (the
# euro sign in WeeklyAnalysisGenerate / RevenueTools), and rewritten line
# endings break re-import into the VBE.
*.bas -text diff
